05. FIRESTORE SECURITY — CRITICAL
==================================================

Review and rewrite Firestore Security Rules where necessary.

Default security policy:

DENY ACCESS UNLESS EXPLICITLY AUTHORIZED.

Never use unrestricted rules.

Never use:

allow read, write: if true;

Never rely on:

allow read, write: if request.auth != null;

as the complete production authorization policy.

Implement collection-specific and document-specific permissions.

