- Access unauthorized institution records.

ADMIN PERMISSIONS:

Only the verified Platform Admin can perform authorized global administrative operations.

Validate ownership and permissions independently.

FIELD VALIDATION:

For important writes:

- Validate document fields.
- Validate field types.
- Validate allowed values.
- Validate document ownership.
- Validate institution references.
- Validate immutable fields.
- Reject unexpected privileged fields.

Protect against client-side privilege escalation.

Use schema validation on the backend as well.

IMPORTANT FIREBASE ADMIN SDK RULE:

Server-side Firebase Admin SDK operations bypass Firestore Security Rules.

Therefore:

Every Admin SDK endpoint must independently validate:
- Authenticated identity.
